ery  nice pictures showing sex also they're  fruiting body it resembles a sack but it  also reproduce will produce haploid  spores by the process of meiosis and the  haploid spores are often released into  the air many sac fungi are edible and  considered a delicacy in in parts of the  world the picture shows crispy veal  sweetbreads filled with truffles looks  very appetizing very delicious  so in this picture we have the final  name of the spore producing structure if  I were to ask you on a test what do we  call the spore producing structure of a  sack fungi here is your answer the sport  producing structures of sack fungi are  called a sky a sky is plural if I were  to ask you the other version of the  question if I were to say which fungi  creates spores and structures known as a  sky I hope you would say oh that's the  sack fungi and when we wrap up these  notes here's a friend from a few months  ago called lichen if you remember lichen  from our ecology chapter we mentioned  they're often called a pioneer species  because they can grow in rocks we also  mentioned that they are a great example  of a mutualistic relationship to  organisms living in a close relationship  where they both benefit the two  organisms are fungus and algae and the  reason this is a great example of  mutualism where they both benefit is  because when you look at them and you  figure out what do they gain well the  fungus because it's a decomposer and it  does external digestion the fungus can  partially digest the algae and obtain  nutrients you might think well isn't  this a parasitic relationship because  the algae is being harmed well remember  that algae need a home to live in they  need a moist environment and that's one  of the advantages that the algae obtains  from the fungus Moisture is trapped  inside the hyphae also the algae has  substance to grow upon algae can't  really grow on bare rock but the fungus  can and so in this case they absolutely  do both benefit the algae would could  not even exist without the benefit of  the fungus  okay so now that we've reached the end  go ahead and pause the video and try to  answer these questions on a separate  sheet of paper if you're in my class I'd  be happy to check your answers either  before class or after class one day so  go ahead and pause the video and try to  complete these good luck
 

